     Welcome to UseNet and networking!  First you need to choose a network
address.  This is how other people address Netmail to you, using your net
address.  Your address is made tacking the site address onto the end of your
net name, such as newuser@siteadress.domain.

     There are restrictions on what name you can choose, the netname must be
shorter than eight characters long, must contain only lowercase alphanumeric
characters and must not begin with a number.  The netname you choose is that
of your first initial combined with your last name or your first name combined
with your last initial.  Also, you cannot choose any netname already chosen
on this site.

    A netname will be suggested, but you may choose what you wish. After you
have a netname, you will be let into the Meta-UseNet network shell.  A '?'
at any prompt will give you a menu of all the commands available at that
prompt.
